#
# Plasma Fusion field log: records the problems Plasma Fusion meets in daily use and keeps them apart
# from the noise of development (docs/parts/fieldlog.md in the Plasma Fusion sources).
#
#   plasma-fusion-fieldlog run                 record until stopped (plasma-fusion-fieldlog.service)
#   plasma-fusion-fieldlog digest [DATE]       write and print the digest of DATE (YYYY-MM-DD, today,
#                                              yesterday; default today)
#   plasma-fusion-fieldlog status              what is recorded today, the service, the state
#   plasma-fusion-fieldlog install [--share DIR]
#                                              copy this tool to ~/.local/libexec/plasma-fusion/,
#                                              write ~/.config/systemd/user/plasma-fusion-fieldlog.service
#                                              from the template next to it, enable and start it
#   plasma-fusion-fieldlog remove              stop, disable and remove the unit and the copy (the
#                                              recorded state stays)
#
# What "run" records, one JSON event per line in events-YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl (local day):
#   - crashes: coredumpctl --json=short every minute (and a few seconds after the journal shows a
#     core dump), each new dump's journal record read once; classes session (Plasma and Plasma Fusion
#     components, anything in the session's session.slice), app (app.slice), other (outside the
#     session) and tooling (a coding agent's marker in the environment or in a process sharing the
#     cgroup, a build/scratch/test path, a container cgroup, a private test session). Session and app
#     crashes get "coredumpctl info" saved in crashes/ at once (core files rotate). Core files are
#     never touched.
#   - session events: plasmashell and kwin_wayland restarts (the session's processes, selected by
#     their cgroup under user@UID.service), logins and logouts, suspend and resume (the boot-time
#     clock against the monotonic clock), screen and lid changes (sysfs, and the plasmafusion-snap KWin
#     script), posture changes (the plasmafusion-tablet KWin script), failed or crashed plasma-* user
#     units.
#   - Plasma Fusion errors: QML/JavaScript errors and warnings whose file or text belongs to Plasma
#     Fusion, the Plasma Fusion tools' warnings, the login check's runs (its gate.log); other
#     plasmashell and KWin warnings only as counts per normalised text.
#   - resources: plasmashell and kwin_wayland RSS, RssAnon and CPU every minute; hourly min, mean,
#     max; a memory snapshot (memsnap/) on a jump of 60 MiB within a minute; an event for 60 % of a
#     core or more for two minutes.
# Repeats of an event are counted, not written again: the first is written at once, the count of
# the repeats every hour and at the end. The day's digest (digest-YYYY-MM-DD.md) is written
# every hour, at the end of the day and when the service stops; with PF_FIELDLOG_SHARE a copy goes to
# that directory as digest-YYYY-MM-DD-HOST.md. 30 days and PF_FIELDLOG_MAX_MB (100) MiB are kept.
#
# Privacy: local files only. Environments are read for the names of agent markers and nothing else
# is kept of them; window titles, notification texts and clipboard contents are not recorded (keyed
# values and long quoted strings are cut out of every kept line; other programs' lines are kept only
# as normalised counts).
#
# Settings (environment): PF_FIELDLOG_SHARE, PF_FIELDLOG_MAX_MB, PF_FIELDLOG_KEEP_DAYS,
# PF_FIELDLOG_MARKERS (more marker names, comma separated), PF_FIELDLOG_SINCE (first run only: record
# core dumps from this time, YYYY-MM-DD[THH:MM] local or @EPOCH; default the start of today),
# PF_FIELDLOG_GATE_LOG (default $XDG_STATE_HOME/plasma-fusion/gate.log). For tests:
# PF_FIELDLOG_INTERVAL (60 s), PF_FIELDLOG_RUN_SECONDS, PF_FIELDLOG_PROC, PF_FIELDLOG_SYS,
# PF_FIELDLOG_CGROUP_ROOT.
